The duties of the joint clean community commission shall be to:
(1) Promote public interest in the general improvement of the environment of the city and county;
(2) Initiate, plan, direct and coordinate programs for litter control for the joint clean community system;
(3) Study, investigate and develop plans for improving the health, sanitation, safety, and cleanliness of the city and the county by beautifying the streets, highways, alleys, river and stream beds, lots, yards, and other similar places in the city and county;
(4) Aid in the prevention of fires, diseases and other casualties by the removal and elimination of trash and other debris from the streets, highways, alleys, lots, yards, plots and other similar places;
(5) Encourage the placing, planting and/or preservation of trees, flowers, plants, shrubbery and other objects or ornamentation in the city and county;
(6) Protect song birds and other wild fowl;
(7) Advise and recommend plans to other agencies of the city and county for the beautification of the city and county;
(8) Otherwise promote public interest in the general improvement of the environment of the city and county;
provided, however, that nothing in this section shall be construed to abridge or change the powers and duties of other commissions, departments, boards and other like agencies of the city and county.
(Ord. No. 380, § 1, 11-8-79)

